{"id":"c5f78c34-9031-4261-8992-36b41c3c7602","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-08-31T21:12:34.431Z","createdBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-31T21:12:34.431Z","lastModifiedBy":"bill.marsland@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 3","sequence":3,"activity":{"id":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","type":"activity","sequence":0,"group":{"id":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","type":"discover","name":null,"sequence":1,"subgroups":[{"id":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"Discover","steps":[{"id":"744c1f93-135e-4fa6-9567-67bfaafdd351","hints":null,"senseiHelp":null,"instructions":null,"text":"<p>Watch this video to learn about using single and nested loops in your projects to run a chunk of code until a specific condition is met or while a specific condition is true!</p>","type":"textMedia","image":null,"videoUrl":"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/videos/YellowBelt-8.mp4","mediaType":"video","questions":[{"hint":"How might a [for index] loop be used in a project?","type":"multi-select","title":"<p>[Select all that apply]&nbsp; A [for index] loop can be useful because it can:</p>","answers":[{"text":"Place sprites in rows and columns.","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Repeat code an infinite number of times.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Run code without using the index of an array.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Repeat code a given number of times.","isCorrect":true}],"wordbank":null,"statements":null,"useWordbank":false,"correctResponse":"Remember, a [for index] loop repeats code for a number of times using an index. It helped place a specific number of plates across multiple rows!"}],"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"38f74b6c-4257-48a7-8d15-2f0397022c20","hints":null,"senseiHelp":null,"instructions":null,"text":"Please update text.","type":"quiz","image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":"video","questions":[{"hint":"How many times will this loop run if it begins counting at 0?","type":"single-select","title":"<p>How many times will the code in this loop run?</p><p>&nbsp;<span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" height=\"64\" width=\"141\"></span></p>","answers":[{"text":"5","isCorrect":true},{"text":"3","isCorrect":false},{"text":"4","isCorrect":false},{"text":"0","isCorrect":false}],"wordbank":null,"statements":null,"useWordbank":false,"correctResponse":"In coding, you begin counting at 0, so this [for index] loop will run 5 times!"}],"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"44cd495d-9ed9-4934-a523-0c0db858723b","hints":null,"senseiHelp":null,"instructions":null,"text":"Please update text.","type":"quiz","image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":"video","questions":[{"hint":"What determines when a [while] loop will start and stop running?","type":"single-select","title":"<p>When does a [while] loop run?</p>","answers":[{"text":"While a certain condition is false","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Only at the beginning of a program","isCorrect":false},{"text":"While a certain condition is true","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Only during a birthday party","isCorrect":false}],"wordbank":null,"statements":null,"useWordbank":false,"correctResponse":"A [while] loop will repeat a chunk of code while a condition is true: while there are guests without cake, keep putting cake on plates! "}],"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"c4431f9f-8c88-49eb-b5d0-58de3fc67cdb","hints":null,"senseiHelp":null,"instructions":null,"text":"Please update text.","type":"quiz","image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":"video","questions":[{"hint":"What happens if there is no “stop” condition for a [while] loop?","type":"single-select","title":"<p>[while] loops will continue to run, unless they have a “stop” condition.&nbsp;</p>","answers":[{"text":"True","isCorrect":true},{"text":"False","isCorrect":false}],"wordbank":null,"statements":null,"useWordbank":false,"correctResponse":"If there are still pieces of cake, I will continue to pass out pieces of cake. The [while] loop requires a condition to say “stop when there are no more guests without cake.”"}],"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"aeeee74c-7432-42a9-bb58-af957105dbd7","hints":null,"senseiHelp":null,"instructions":null,"text":"Please update text.","type":"quiz","image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":"video","questions":[{"hint":"Which option uses a [while] loop to perform an action while a certain condition is true?","type":"single-select","title":"<p>We can use a [while] loop to:</p>","answers":[{"text":"Place plates on a table in multiple rows.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Continue passing out cake slices, while there are guests without cake.","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Welcome guests into the house.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Continue passing out cake slices, as long as all guests have a piece of cake.","isCorrect":false}],"wordbank":null,"statements":null,"useWordbank":false,"correctResponse":"Remember, a [while] loop will continue to run while a certain condition is true!"}],"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Nested Loops!","project":null,"peerReview":false,"mediaFileId":"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/videos/YellowBelt-8.mp4","introduction":"<p>Watch this video to learn about using single and nested loops in your projects to run a chunk of code until a specific condition is met or while a specific condition is true!</p>","lowThreshold":0,"hasLowThreshold":false,"numberOfReviews":0,"validationItems":null,"passingThreshold":0,"hasPassingThreshold":false,"codingStep":{"hints":null,"project":null,"senseiHelp":null,"validationItems":null},"senseiStep":null,"planningStep":null,"ninjaRequirements":null,"status":false}],"status":false},"status":false},"description":"<p><strong>You’ve reached Level 3 of Green Belt!</strong> In this level, you’ll learn more about [for index] and [while] loops. These loops can be used to control the placement of sprites on a tilemap and make something happen while a certain condition is true. Here are the achievements you’ll unlock in Level 3:</p>","mustCompletePrevious":true,"badges":[{"url":"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/icons/GB_Level%203-50.webp","title":"Around and Around","description":"<p>Use advanced loops that offer more control options to repeat code in a project.</p>"},{"url":"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/icons/GB_3%20-%20Card%20Catalog.webp","title":"Card Catalog","description":"<p>Use a loop that counts from 0 to a given number to repeat a section of code.</p>"},{"url":"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/icons/GB_3%20-%20Waiting%20for%20Things%20to%20Change.webp","title":"Waiting for Things to Change","description":"<p>Use a loop that will repeat a section of code while a condition is true.</p>"}],"activeGroupId":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","activeSubGroupId":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","activeActivityId":"bf8cfbc3-2c1c-428c-90f8-89e578a37dcc","status":false,"courseName":"Green Belt"},"relationShips":{"data":{"programId":"1b04b70e-39e3-4a19-968c-3e7cccc0dd47","courseId":"b9515aae-8a21-4e94-95c5-c25268360ba5"}}}
